+
+The frozen `2a3ed25668dbb2dab60400a18f4ba9ac71a35606` broad browser job [111397871961](https://github.com/sveltery/base/actions/runs/37189259376/job/111397871961) passed 2,643 cases and failed the older authored completed-close case: expected one false completion, observed two. Its [exact predecessor body](receipts/completed-close-predecessor.spec.ts.txt), [lossless connector JSON](receipts/2a3ed25-broad-failed-api-raw.json.gz) and [decoded raw log](receipts/2a3ed25-broad-failed-api-raw.log.gz) are retained. The raw decoded log SHA256 is `6a74fb0c7899a18f7fd142fcacee7385278a15b236d2ba52ed9f906a7fd623a2`; this remains a failed run.
+
+Original [`useOpenStateTransitions`](https://github.com/mui/base-ui/blob/47b40521eab921c2756bf9bdb0b0f07fbfdb8c8c/packages/react/src/utils/popups/popupStoreUtils.ts#L554) enables close completion while mounted, closed and not deferred. Completion calls `forceUnmount`, sets mounted false and emits `onOpenChangeComplete(false)`. Original [`DialogPopup`](https://github.com/mui/base-ui/blob/47b40521eab921c2756bf9bdb0b0f07fbfdb8c8c/packages/react/src/dialog/popup/DialogPopup.tsx#L97) disables FocusManager when mounted becomes false. The [`FloatingFocusManager` cleanup](https://github.com/mui/base-ui/blob/47b40521eab921c2756bf9bdb0b0f07fbfdb8c8c/packages/react/src/floating-ui-react/components/FloatingFocusManager.tsx#L750) then queues focus return. The native popup-store, Popup and FocusManager preserve that ownership and order. This fixture's returned-focus wait follows completion of its first close; reopening starts a new cycle.
+
+The paired actual Original/native [DOM lifecycle probes](../../packages/base/tests/dom/dialog-source-business.test.ts) control popup animation promises. Resolving a held close returns focus and emits the first false callback; reopening and closing emits a second. Reopening before the held exit resolves aborts that incomplete close, yielding only one final false callback. The actual Original/native [physical browser pairs](../../tests/browser/dialog-motion-source.spec.ts) retain a nonempty paused animation, ending style, accessible Popup and retained focus before interrupted reopening. Their strict sequence remains `[true, true, false]`. The separate completed pair requires `[true, false, true, false]`. Historical secured official Chromium run [37163598560/job111321908271](https://github.com/sveltery/base/actions/runs/37163598560/job/111321908271) at Dialog `a933563` passed all four physical pairs and all 56 focused cases; its broad step was canceled and is not a broad pass.
+
+Under Root's precise lease, [dialog.spec.ts](../../tests/browser/dialog.spec.ts) copies the exact proved canonical Dialog completed-case body: title, lifecycle comment and expected count two. Its full interaction sequence, returned-focus wait, accessible/ending/open/hidden predicates and timeout stay intact. The separate interrupted pairs remain strict. The canonical motion fixture stays SHA256 `ad4d335f410e673f32389daae7c7a5df0278753d3053c60e811c009fec08362a`. No product animation algorithm, cancellation rule, timeout, retry, security setting or parity credit changes. Fresh successor hosted focused and broad execution remains required.
